 ROUND:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C round(x) - real to integer, the compiler's retired ROUND
C
C Calling convention (single argument, in ACC):
C   ACC = the real value
C   M13 = return link
C
C   int round(float) assembler;
C
C The sequence the mcROUND macro emitted: add a half, then let
C the alignment against the integer zero shift the fraction out,
C which floors.  The closing AEX strips the exponent the
C alignment leaves behind, an integer word here carrying none;
C it also leaves the mode register at 7, the integer mode
C compiled code expects on return.
C===========================================================
                ,NTR ,7      . suppress normalization and rounding
            1   ,A+X ,23B    . =R0.5
            1   ,A+X ,11B    . =I0  align: the fraction is gone
            1   ,AEX ,11B    . =I0  strip the integer exponent
            13  ,UJ  ,
                ,END ,
